<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="22.1" level="1">Education</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="9" level="2">School Property</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="2" level="3">School Buildings</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>22.1-135</section_number>
	<catch_line>Health and decency</catch_line>
	<text>
		No public school shall be allowed in any building which is not in such condition and provided with such conveniences as are required by a due regard for decency and health.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, §§ 22-97, 22-157; 1954, c. 291; 1959, Ex. Sess., c. 79, § 1; 1968, c. 501; 1971, Ex. Sess., c. 161; 1975, cc. 308, 328; 1978, c. 430; 1980, c. 559.</history>
</law>
